# Generation Pipeline

## Stage 1 — Parse OpenAPI

Input

```
openapi.json

or

openapi.yaml
```

Responsibilities

- Parse OpenAPI specification
- Validate specification
- Resolve `$ref`
- Extract endpoints
- Extract schemas
- Extract authentication
- Normalize specification

Output

```
OpenApiDocument
```

---

## Stage 2 — Internal Intermediate Model

The parser converts the OpenAPI document into an internal representation used throughout the generator.

The generator never reads OpenAPI directly.

Example:

```
OpenAPI

↓

Internal Intermediate Model

↓

Endpoint Definitions

↓

Tool Definitions
```

The IIM contains

- Endpoints
- Parameters
- Request Bodies
- Response Schemas
- Authentication
- Tags
- Models

This architecture allows future support for multiple input formats while keeping the generator unchanged.

---

## Stage 3 — Code Generation

Input

```
Internal Intermediate Model
```

Responsibilities

- Generate imports
- Generate MCP server
- Generate tool files
- Generate authentication
- Generate schemas
- Generate project structure

The code generation engine uses

- ts-morph
- Handlebars templates

Output

```
TypeScript Source Files
```

---

## Stage 4 — Generate Project Assets

Generate project files

```
package.json

tsconfig.json

bunfig.toml

README.md

.gitignore

.env.example
```

using reusable Handlebars templates.

---

## Stage 5 — Validation

After generation

```
Generate Project

↓

bun install

↓

Type Check

↓

Build

↓

Start MCP Server

↓

Initialize MCP

↓

List Tools

↓

Execute Sample Tool

↓

Validation Passed
```

Only validated projects are considered successfully generated.

